  "solution": {
    "text": "The average power consumed in an AC circuit is given by<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#981;</mi></math><br /><br />Where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#981;</mi></math> is phase angle and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are the peak values of voltage and current respectively.<br /><br />Given, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>V</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>A</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>200</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>200</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>"
  }
